Here is an example of how you can use a while loop to call a function multiple times:
```
int count = 0;
while (count < 5) {
  myFunction();
  count++;
}
```
This will call the `myFunction()` function 5 times, and the `count` variable will be set to 5 after the loop is finished.

It is important to note that the `while` loop will continue to run until the condition is no longer true. In this case, the loop will continue to run until the `count` variable is greater than or equal to 5.

